# Do not delete — this file is what puts the dashboard in the published package.
#
# `package.json` allowlists `web/dist`, but with no `.npmignore` here npm falls
# back to `web/.gitignore`, which ignores `dist/` (correctly — build output does
# not belong in git). The allowlist does not override a nested ignore file, so
# the tarball shipped with no dashboard at all and `baton serve` answered every
# installed user with its own "dashboard not built" error.
#
# Listing node_modules alone replaces that fallback: `files` decides what ships
# and nothing here vetoes it. Guarded by test/packaging.test.ts.
node_modules/
